Rise Employability workshop – 3 hours [3rd Item]

Rise is an initiative that aims to boost social mobility in the UK by helping young people develop the essential skills that businesses need. The Seven Steps to Rise workshop consists of a carousel of challenges designed for students aged 14-15.

Benefits

•	Increase Confidence & Credibility 
•	Improved Communication & Collaboration
•	Short Commitment
•	Educational Impact 

Button – Link Pending



Opening Doors to Opportunities – In–Office Edition 2-3 hours  [4th Item]

Opening Doors to Opportunities invites schools into our offices across the UK, as part of our commitment we’ve made to give one million young people the opportunity to develop their skills by 2030.

We’re asking colleagues to help us to ‘open doors,’ by supporting 2-hour workplace visits at offices across the UK. Volunteers support the students with their activities and talk to them about working somewhere like KPMG. You do not need to have experience with young people or specific numeracy knowledge as you will be fully supported throughout. We are looking for volunteers of any grade and area of the business.

Benefits 

•	Short Commitment 
•	Improved Communication & Collaboration 
•	Build professional Networks 
•	Increase Confidence & Credibility 
•	Educational Impact 

Register now
